h of the following could be $f(t)$, where $u$ denotes the unit step function?" 13194139534716 false] [17592186152481 1145 "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/9fb8c20672705e9d68e69d32e7ff3499ec71560e10aa85136b3f3ad75c5fb5ed.png)\n\nNotice that to transform $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we reflect $y=u(t)$ in the $y$-axis, which gives $y=u(-t).$\n\n- Next, we scale $y=u(-t)$ by a factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=2u(-t).$\n\n- There is no horizontal shift or offset.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=2u(-t).$" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305158 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305159 13194139534716 true] [17592186305158 1089 "q-331185" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305158 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534716 true] [17592186305158 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/6f80319af7f362c2a902853687670a9dab8e88778521147942dfb9a0d9872b75.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t),$ where $u$ denotes the unit step function?" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305158 1113 #uuid "667d57dc-7eb9-57bc-b685-cfc00950512e" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305158 1145 "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/4f7a1a32f5c639ec0a9433fc6d330e5ea9f8ed6fa1602441b54c9158bb69f63e.png)\n\nNotice that to transform the function $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we shift $y=u(t)$ by one unit to the right, giving $y=u(t-1).$\n\n- Then, we scale by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=2u(t-1).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=2u(t-1).$" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305160 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305161 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305162 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305163 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305164 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1041 "selection" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305162 13194139534716 true] [17592186305159 1110 #uuid "078e107b-7b29-5a1f-9685-66391c09a6b2" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305160 1034 "u(t-1)+1" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534716 true] [17592186305160 1111 #uuid "ffbb67b0-cdb6-5a80-a77c-d557c3a1dad4" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305161 1034 "2u(t+1)" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534716 true] [17592186305161 1111 #uuid "9897b502-a26a-5ea2-b545-f024841ec582" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305162 1034 "2u(t-1)" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534716 true] [17592186305162 1111 #uuid "5da9e907-aa4f-5f60-8463-5d39b6a89900" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305163 1034 "u(t+1)+1" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534716 true] [17592186305163 1111 #uuid "8af50beb-c843-54f4-8247-547147ee4e88" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305164 1034 "2u(t+2)" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534716 true] [17592186305164 1111 #uuid "184e7c5f-3d47-5706-9076-adb0c3a1e6a0" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305165 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305166 13194139534716 true] [17592186305165 1089 "q-331230" 13194139534716 true] [17592186305165 1091 #edb/ref 17